            <ArticleTitle>Enantioselective Total Synthesis and Structure Confirmation of the Natural Dimeric Tetrahydroxanthenone Dicerandrol C.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2299-2302</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/chem.201700020</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The first enantioselective total synthesis of natural dicerandrol C (1 c) as its enantiomer containing a dimeric tetrahydroxanthenone skeleton is described starting from the enantiopure chromane 6 which was obtained through a Wacker-type cyclization with &gt;99 % ee. For the formation of the dimeric skeleton a palladium-catalyzed Suzuki reaction was used. The synthesis allowed the confirmation of the absolute configuration of the dicerandrols.</AbstractText>
